.\" man/man3/Docv::Layout.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Layout" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Layout \- Turns a \fB\%Document\fR into lines of cells for a given width.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBclass Docv::Layout\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Turns a \fB\%Document\fR into lines of cells for a given width. Wrapped layout
fills paragraphs to the width; unwrapped layout puts each paragraph on a
single line. Unfilled text and tables never wrap.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBLINK\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
LINK = /(?<![\ew.\e\-])([A\-Za\-z_][\ew.:+\e\-@]*)\e(([0\-9][a\-zA\-Z0\-9]*|n|l)\e)/
.EE
.RE
.RE
.TP 4
\fBQUOTE_BAR = \(aq\[u2502]\(aq\fR
Drawn at each \fB\%Block#bars\fR column, and across a \fB\%BlockKind::Rule\fR.
.PP
\fBRULE = \(aq\[u2500]\(aq\fR
.SH "CONSTRUCTORS"
.PP
\fBdef self.new(document : Document)\fR
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.append(cells : Array(Cell), cluster : String, style : UInt16) : Nil\fR
Appends the cell(s) of a grapheme cluster.
.SH "INSTANCE METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef document : Document\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef flow(pieces : Array(Piece), first : Int32, rest : Int32, limit : Int32, fill : Bool, tabs : Tabs, start : Row | Nil = nil) : Array(Row)\fR
Places \fIpieces\fR into rows: the first row starts at \fIfirst\fR (or
continues \fIstart\fR), wrapped rows at \fIrest\fR, filling up to \fIlimit\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef footer_line(width : Int32) : Line | Nil\fR
The page footer for \fIwidth\fR columns: the source, the date centered and
the reference. \fB\%nil\fR when the document has no title, and for Markdown.
.TP 4
\fBdef header_line(width : Int32) : Line | Nil\fR
The page header for \fIwidth\fR columns: the reference, the manual title
centered and the reference again. \fB\%nil\fR when the document has no
title, and for Markdown.
.TP 4
\fBdef lines(width : Int32, wrap : Bool = true, header : Bool = true, footer : Bool = true) : Array(Line)\fR
Lays out the document for \fIwidth\fR columns. With \fIheader\fR the lines
start with the page header (\fB\%header_line\fR) and a blank line; with
\fIfooter\fR they end with a blank line and the page footer
(\fB\%footer_line\fR).
.TP 4
\fBdef tokenize(spans : Array(Span)) : Array(Piece)\fR
Splits spans into words, blank runs and tabs.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/layout.cr
